 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Definitely. Lots of people do it. You might want get a small desk or stand up though. Sitting down while you can helps a lot of people after surgery. Then be smart about it. Take short breaks every hour or so, stand up and move around. Then lean on something firm and put your feet up if you have chair footstool. There are also tiny desks and standing desks that fit in a small space. Try sitting on an exercise ball at your desk. It helps you keep moving even while you' working.",
